{"game": "arma-3", "language": "english", "appid": 107410, "month": "2025-05", "window": 2, "start_date": 1746662400, "end_date": 1747353599, "month_true_total": 484, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 11:19:28 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "194975903", "author": {"steamid": "76561198090271278", "personaname": "☣Mercy☣", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198090271278/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 7276, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 5927, "last_played": 1750110359, "avatar": "018df4487c4753410619e93ed19f867caa619b0c"}, "language": "english", "review": "Man, Arma 3 is such a mixed bag for me. I’ve sunk 99.5 hours into it, and I can see why it’s a military sim lover’s dream. The realism is insane—like, the way you can plan missions, the huge maps, and the attention to detail with the vehicles and weapons is top-notch. I love how you can jump into a helicopter, mess around with mods, or just go on a massive multiplayer operation with friends. It feels so immersive when everything clicks.\r\n\r\nBut honestly, it’s not all perfect. The learning curve is brutal. I spent the first few hours just trying to figure out the controls, and even then, I kept dying because I couldn’t spot enemies hiding in bushes. The AI can be dumb as a rock sometimes, either standing there or randomly one-shotting you from a mile away. Also, the game can be a glitchy mess—my squad got stuck in a rock once, and we had to restart the whole mission. It’s not the most polished experience, and you really need a good PC to run it smoothly.\r\n\r\nOverall, I’d say Arma 3 is awesome if you’ve got the patience for it and love military strategy, but it’s definitely not for everyone. I’m still gonna hop back in for more chaos, though!", "timestamp_created": 1747352595, "timestamp_updated": 1747352595, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.